      ],
      "explanation": "The component comments assign monotonically increasing commitment from voter progress and require reaching the first index of the leader's term. These attributed responsibilities support the local obligation independently of its sorting implementation. The new caller material also shows one commitment object initialized during leader setup and consumed by leaderLoop. Provisionally, the obligation applies to this component scope.",
      "alternatives": "Previously established commitIndex may remain unchanged after voter replacement without acquiring fresh support from the replacement map. Stored progress need only be nondecreasing when updated by match, not across removal and later reintroduction.",
      "counterexample_reasoning": "A same-instance match call that lowered stored progress, or an advancement lacking current-map majority support, would contradict the selected responsibility. A reset caused by removing and later reintroducing a voter would not violate the match-report clause.",
      "limitations": [
        "This is a source-based interpretation, not an executed check.",
        "The positive interpretation repeats the substance of issue 816ba277d65a4acb950f4454cfe49ab9; no separate resolution is claimed for that stored issue."
      ]
